    "field": "Ecosystem ecology",
    "problem": "The relative importance of climate-induced changes in plant phenology versus physiology on annual gross primary productivity (GPP) variability is unclear, making it challenging to disentangle their respective contributions to carbon uptake under climate change.",
    "method": "A statistical model is used to evaluate the relative contributions of plant physiology (maximum daily GPP) and phenology (growing season start/end) to the trend and inter-annual variability of annual gross primary productivity.",
    "task": "The task is to evaluate the relative contributions of plant physiology (maximum productivity) and phenology (growing season timing) to the long-term trend and inter-annual variability of gross primary productivity in North America using a statistical model.",
